        {
            "id": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/my-deaf-mom.html",
            "url": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/my-deaf-mom.html",
            "title": "My First Job",
            "summary": "She lived her life with an immature desire. Dancing and singing, her&hellip;",
            "content_html": "<div class=\"align-center\">She lived her life with an immature desire.<br>Dancing and singing, her face lit a room.<br>But like a firecracker before the boom,<br>many often held their breath while by her.</div>\n<div class=\"align-center\"> </div>\n<div class=\"align-center\">I remember once, while near that line of fire,<br>I blushed, a boy of five, from her strong fume.<br>Her lips spewing forth in an obscene plume,<br>while she alone would not hear the deafening ire.</div>\n<div class=\"align-center\"> </div>\n<div class=\"align-center\">Then I’d relay the circumspect reply,<br>from a confused face speaking through her child,<br>as my mother lit a fresh cigarette.</div>\n<div class=\"align-center\"> </div>\n<div class=\"align-center\">Rewinding the tape with her careful eye,<br>she watched me imitate the words which riled,<br>never showing me a small sign of regret.</div>",
            "image": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/media/posts/24/signlanguage.jpg",
            "author": {
                "name": "Kevin Kwilinski"
            },
            "tags": [
            ],
            "date_published": "2026-09-28T21:13:36-04:00",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-05T22:14:27-04:00"
        },
        {
            "id": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/bread.html",
            "url": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/bread.html",
            "title": "Bread",
            "summary": "I smell the bread baking and I’m reminded of your soft hands&hellip;",
            "content_html": "<div class=\"align-center\">I smell the bread baking<br>and I’m reminded of your soft hands<br>touching that fleshy dough.<br>You make me hungry.</div>\n<div class=\"align-center\"> </div>\n<div class=\"align-center\">As steam and hot scent<br>escape from the oven door,<br>I see our reflection in the glass.<br>My face is covered in sweat.</div>\n<div class=\"align-center\"> </div>\n<div class=\"align-center\">Though you give me a generous slice,<br>hot with salted butter;<br>even while the taste still lingers,<br>I want more.</div>",
            "image": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/media/posts/23/freshly-baked-bread-stockcake.jpg",
            "author": {
                "name": "Kevin Kwilinski"
            },
            "tags": [
            ],
            "date_published": "2026-09-28T21:01:59-04:00",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-04T17:20:33-04:00"
        },
        {
            "id": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/autumn.html",
            "url": "https://words.skylarkfoundry.com/autumn.html",
            "title": "Autumn",
            "summary": "I looked out for you, but frost covered my window. Summer, did&hellip;",
            "content_html": "<p class=\"align-center\">I looked out for you,<br>but frost covered my window.<br>Summer, did you leave?</p>",
